From ce54caed10fd50bbb913fff83e5787b8454d481c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivan Faeton Danishevskyi <faeton@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 22:28:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] AccountsDb: close the CE database on close()

Since the CE database got its own connection (e866ee92, 083147324f7b),
close() only closed the DE one. accounts_ce.db stayed open after a
user was stopped and vold removed the CE key with busy files.
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/accounts/AccountsDb.java     | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/accounts/AccountsDb.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/accounts/AccountsDb.java
index 338aee3aafcd..65d6ec4e6c6f 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/accounts/AccountsDb.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/accounts/AccountsDb.java
@@ -1455,6 +1455,10 @@ class AccountsDb implements AutoCloseable {
     @Override
     public void close() {
         mDeDatabase.close();
+        // CE database has its own connection, keep it from holding files of a stopped user open
+        if (mCeDatabase != null) {
+            mCeDatabase.close();
+        }
     }
 
     static void deleteDbFileWarnIfFailed(File dbFile) {
-- 
2.39.5

